{"nodes": [{"id": "prd_coven_mcp_prd", "label": "coven-mcp PRD", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "prd_tool_surface", "label": "Tool Surface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "prd_coven_read_output", "label": "coven_read_output", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The hardest component: bounded polling of the events route with a streaming sanitizer state machine, because output.data is raw PTY text with ANSI escapes split across events, payload_json is double-encoded JSON, and every stop must map to exactly one documented tuple so callers can branch deterministically."}, {"id": "prd_resume_token", "label": "Resume Token", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "FR-17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "HMAC-SHA-256-signed base64url payload {v, sessionId, afterSeq, pendingRawB64}; null afterSeq is the explicit pre-first-event state so no sentinel is invented; pending state is compacted (current line + incomplete escape) so a CR-heavy progress bar can never grow state unboundedly; UTF-16LE encoding so a chunk split inside a surrogate pair survives; per-process secret means tokens intentionally die on restart, with afterSeq=lastSeq as the documented recovery."}, {"id": "prd_authority_boundary", "label": "Authority Boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deny by default (unset allowlist means read-only); misconfiguration aborts startup loudly rather than degrading; write tools authorize the daemon's canonical project_root, never a caller-supplied path; containment is path-component based after symlink resolution; the allowlist is an authorization gate, not a sandbox, and prompt injection is explicitly in the threat model."}, {"id": "prd_error_taxonomy", "label": "Error Taxonomy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Branch on error.code, never message text; only named daemon codes get bespoke handling and the other ~33 fall through to structured UPSTREAM_ERROR so unmapped codes can never become transport errors or leak raw daemon bodies."}, {"id": "prd_health_gate", "label": "Health Gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lazy per-call handshake (cached 1.5s, single-flight) instead of a startup check, so tool discovery stays stable while the daemon is down and daemon restarts never require restarting the MCP client; a capability counts only when exactly true because health advertises string-valued capabilities."}, {"id": "prd_normalized_shapes", "label": "Normalized Shapes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "prd_memory_excerpt_policy", "label": "Memory Excerpt Policy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "FR-9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The daemon route includes bounded excerpts, so blindly forwarding it is content disclosure; excerpts are blanked by default, forwarded only under COVEN_MCP_INCLUDE_MEMORY_EXCERPTS=true, and revealRequired or non-public classification forces redaction even then."}, {"id": "prd_acceptance_criteria", "label": "Acceptance Criteria", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "prd_coven_mcp_prd", "target": "plan_build_plan", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "header", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_coven_mcp_prd", "target": "prd_tool_surface", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_coven_mcp_prd", "target": "prd_coven_read_output", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_coven_mcp_prd", "target": "prd_authority_boundary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.4", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_coven_mcp_prd", "target": "prd_error_taxonomy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_coven_mcp_prd", "target": "prd_health_gate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_coven_mcp_prd", "target": "prd_acceptance_criteria", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_tool_surface", "target": "prd_normalized_shapes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "PRD.md", "source_location": "\u00a76.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prd_tool_surface", "target": "prd_memory_exce